{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowIsHecke","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowIsHecke","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_eq_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_eq_smul","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L83-L88","doc":"The vacuum-row vector is a nonzero rescaling of the quantum-dimension vector:\n`S_{0λ} = (1/D) · d_q(λ)`.  Records that `bwS0 ∝ d_q` with the single\nnormalisation `1/D` (no per-block freedom) — the content the geometric\nrealisations were trying, and failing, to reproduce independently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L74-L81","doc":"**The keystone value step (the \"what\"), sorry-free.** The vacuum-row ratio\nto the vacuum entry is exactly the quantum dimension:\n`S_{0λ} / S_{00} = d_q(λ)`.  This is `bwS0` recognised as the Verlinde\nvacuum row of the SU_q(2)/Hecke modular category (redirect iii). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_vac","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L70-L72","doc":"`S_{00} = 1 / D` — the vacuum entry (its quantum dimension is `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L67-L68","doc":"The S-matrix vacuum-row entry `S_{0λ} = d_q(λ) / D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.D_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.D_ne","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The total quantum dimension is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.d_vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.d_vac","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The vacuum object has quantum dimension `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.vac","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The vacuum (trivial object) label. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.D","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Total quantum dimension (`√(Σ d_λ²)` downstream; abstract here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.d","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Quantum dimension of each fusion block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow","kind":"structure","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean#L46-L61","doc":"A modular S-matrix **vacuum row** over a fusion-label type `ι`: the entries\nare the quantum dimensions `d` normalised by the total quantum dimension `D`,\nwith a distinguished vacuum label `vac` of quantum dimension `1`.  `D` is\ncarried abstractly (its value `√(Σ_λ d_λ²)` is archimedean and lives\ndownstream); only `D ≠ 0` is used here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}